#X text 480 20 bridge_sliceWriter: REPLACES js_slice_writer_stub. Inlet 0 takes the EXACT SAME messages the original Max js object took (set_vocals_time <f>\, write_vocals\, set_meta_vocals_bpm <f>\, write_meta_vocals\, set_track_name <name>\, set_bpm_gate <f>\, trackExists <name>\, forgetTrack <name>\, reset / reset_vocals / reset_melo / reset_bass / reset_drum -- see slice_writer_bridge.js for the full list) -- unchanged from upstream's wiring\, since Pd's message-selector-first-in-list convention is identical to Max's. [pd packOSC] treats the message's own selector as the OSC address and the rest of the list as the OSC args -- verified against the official Pd-vanilla OSC transition example (danomatika/BangYourHead\, mrpeach-to-vanilla-osc.pd)\, not guessed. [list prepend send] -> [list trim] -> [netsend -u -b] is the standard vanilla idiom for actually transmitting the formatted bytes (same source)., f 380;
#X text 480 280 3 outlets\, matching outlets 1/2/3 of the original js object (outlet 0 -- replace/clear to a Max dict object with no Pd equivalent -- is intentionally NOT reproduced here\, see CONVERSION_NOTES.md "spat_fx_router.js dropped..." section successor entry and slice_writer_bridge.js's own header comment for why): outlet 0 = total slice count (float\, was outlet 1)\, outlet 1 = last slice ID (symbol\, was outlet 2)\, outlet 2 = trackExists/set_track_name skip-flag (float 0 or 1\, was outlet 3)., f 380;
#X text 480 400 Start the bridge alongside Pd: node bridge/slice_writer_bridge.js --data-dir /path/to/EBYS/data --recv-port 9002 --send-port 9003 (ports must match the netsend "connect" message and the netreceive port above)., f 380;
